{"question_id": "th-004", "category": "thesis", "question": "What investable thesis do Meridian Tech Daily and Lumina funding news articulate about agent infrastructure?", "expected_answer_keywords": ["inference cost", "sub-$1", "agent"], "forbidden_keywords": [], "expected_doc_keys": ["lumina-small-model-thesis-news", "lumina-inference-funding"], "expected_abstain": false, "notes": "News synthesis plus funding strategic rationale.", "answer": "Based on the provided context, the investable thesis articulated by Meridian Tech and Lumina\u2019s funding announcements centers on the \"small-model inference cost collapse\" fundamentally \"reshaping agent economics\" C5. This thesis posits that aggressively driving down the per-token costs of running AI agents makes large-scale autonomous operations commercially viable. Consequently, this economic shift is attracting significant venture capital to build out specialized infrastructure; for instance, Lumina AI Labs raised an $180 million Series C round specifically to finance an additional 20% reduction in API unit costs C6. Ultimately, the market views deep cost compression in small-model inference as the critical catalyst for scaling and monetizing next-generation agent infrastructure C1.", "abstained": false, "cited_doc_keys": ["lumina-inference-funding", "lumina-small-model-thesis-news"], "retrieved_doc_keys": ["lumina-api-pricing-nov-2025", "lumina-inference-funding", "lumina-mmlu-forecast-expired", "lumina-small-model-thesis-news", "lumina-spark-0-9-deprecation"], "latency_s": 21.37394550256431, "tokens_used": 3480, "question_shape": "multi_doc", "query_intent": "company_strategy_or_funding", "answer_correctness": 0.6666666666666666, "forbidden_violation": false, "evidence_recall_at_k": 1.0, "citation_precision": 1.0, "citation_faithfulness": true, "temporal_correctness": null, "supersession_correctness": null, "abstention_accuracy": true}
